WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
When an economy slows down,

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.560
households tend to trim their spending.

3
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.800
But business spending on new machines,

4
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.360
offices and buildings
can plunge much further.

5
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.520
Then, as the economy recovers,

6
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.480
it can surge back.

7
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.990
Why does business spending swing so
much more than household spending?

8
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.860
In this mission, you'll split
investment into gross and net,

9
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.200
and work out what really
drives firms to invest.

10
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.080
Then you'll move two
sliders in a graph lab,

11
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.370
predict what happens to aggregate demand,

12
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:32.770
and test it.

13
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:37.560
Your mission: explain why investment
swings so much more than consumption.
